```
Reason:
The `ModifiableSolrParams` object (`clientParams`) was initialized without any socket connect or read timeout parameters being set before it was passed to `HttpClientUtil.createClient()`. This omission occurred due to an exception being thrown when attempts were made to set these parameters, which resulted in the connection and read timeouts being ignored.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
clientParams.set(HttpClientUtil.PROP_SO_TIMEOUT, cfg.getDistributedSocketTimeout());
clientParams.set(HttpClientUtil.PROP_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT, cfg.getDistributedConnectionTimeout());
```
Reason:
These statements explicitly set the socket read timeout and connection timeout parameters in the `clientParams` object based on the provided configuration (`cfg`). By correctly applying these timeouts before creating the HTTP client, the bug is resolved, ensuring that the connection and read timeouts are honored in the `UpdateShardHandler`.


